      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "power_supervisor",
        "description": "TPS3703 supervises the regulated 3.3V rail and provides a POWER_GOOD status output via its RESET pin. This module is powered from the regulated VCC_3V3 rail through VDD and monitors that same rail through SENSE, so the supervision threshold applies to the actual LDO output. CT is a timing/configuration node that requires an external passive network in downstream design to define reset/assert timing behavior. MR is an external manual-reset/control input pin provided by the IC; because the brief does not require manual reset functionality, its final bias policy must be resolved during detailed wiring rather than assumed here. RESET is exposed as the module's POWER_GOOD interface; downstream wiring must preserve any output-stage requirements such as pull-up ownership or polarity handling according to the chosen implementation and datasheet behavior.",
        "id": "power_supervisor"
      },
